Article 2 (Establishment and Functions)
(1) The Tax Revenue Estimation Committee (hereinafter referred to as the "Committee") shall be established under the Minister of Finance and Economy to deliberate transparently and objectively on estimates and forecasts of revenues from internal taxes, customs duties, and earmarked taxes.
(2) The Committee shall deliberate on the following matters:
1. Matters concerning the assumptions underlying tax revenue estimates, including economic forecasts;
2. Matters concerning analyses of actual tax revenues and projections thereof;
3. Other matters concerning tax revenue estimates submitted to a meeting by the chairperson of the Committee.
